CORE
main.c
--unwind 3 --refine-concurrency
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
Threads write different bytes of a field-sensitive union: each write must only
assign the fields overlapping its bytes, rather than write back the values of
the others (which a concurrent write to those bytes may have changed).
As test.desc, with the from-read constraints added lazily (--refine-concurrency).
